 e.setAttribute('src','//assets.pinterest.com/js/pinmarklet.js?r='+Math.random()*99999999);
 document.body.appendChild(e);
 " ><span class="swp_count swp_hide"><span class="iconFiller"><span class="spaceManWilly"><i class="sw swp_pinterest_icon"></i><span class="swp_share">Pin</span></span></span></span></a></div></div><input class="jpibfi" type="hidden"><p>Charlotte is a city that knows how to serve up flavor, and nowhere is that more evident than in its top restaurants. From bold bites to comforting classics, these spots deliver the best of what’s on the menu. Here are the 7 best places to experience Charlotte’s vibrant food scene.</p><h2>Which Wich Superior Sandwiches</h2><p>$ | <a href="tel:(704) 504-8267" rel="nofollow">(704) 504-8267</a> | <a href="https://whichwich.olo.express/menu/which-wich-shops-at-rivergate-south" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">WEBSITE</a></p><p><img class="aligncenter br-lazy" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0naHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmcnIHZpZXdCb3g9JzAgMCAwIDAnPjwvc3ZnPg==" data-breeze="https://restaurantobserver.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Which-Wich-Superior-Sandwiches.jpeg"  alt='Which Wich Superior Sandwiches' src='https://restaurantobserver.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Which-Wich-Superior-Sandwiches.jpeg' data-jpibfi-post-excerpt="" data-jpibfi-post-url="https://restaurantobserver.com/restaurants-in-charlotte-nc/" data-jpibfi-post-title="7 Best Restaurants in Charlotte, NC [2026 Updated]" data-jpibfi- ></p><p>There’s something undeniably satisfying about building a sandwich from scratch, and at Which Wich Superior Sandwiches, the process feels like a game of culinary roulette. The roast beef option is a standout, with its tender slices and just the right amount of seasoning. The staff, especially a team member with locs and dark skin who puts good energy into each sandwich, makes the experience feel personal. They’re friendly, attentive, and always ready to help you customize your order.</p><p>The owner’s presence adds a layer of authenticity—keeping things clean and offering a helping hand when needed. The atmosphere is cozy but not too loud, with a simple, modern décor that keeps the focus on the food. Prices are reasonable for the quality, with most sandwiches coming in around $8–$10. It’s the kind of place where you’ll leave feeling satisfied and already thinking about coming back.</p><p><iframe width="100%" height="300" style="border:0;" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed/v1/place?q=place_id:ChIJyzpSdYCQVogRbw1uERNN4Xk&amp;zoom=17&amp;key=AIzaSyDhhWij3suiM7Ju7qOcU66HY61rNBu8JRk"></iframe></p><div style="border-bottom: 1px solid #d9d9d9; margin: 16px 0;"></div><h2>The Cellar at Duckworth&#x27;s</h2><p>$$$ | <a href="tel:(980) 349-4078" rel="nofollow">(980) 349-4078</a> | <a href="http://thecellaratduckworths.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">WEBSITE</a></p><p><img class="aligncenter br-lazy" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0naHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmcnIHZpZXdCb3g9JzAgMCAwIDAnPjwvc3ZnPg==" data-breeze="https://restaurantobserver.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/The-Cellar-at-Duckworths.jpeg"  alt='The Cellar at Duckworth&#x27;s' src='https://restaurantobserver.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/The-Cellar-at-Duckworths.jpeg' data-jpibfi-post-excerpt="" data-jpibfi-post-url="https://restaurantobserver.com/restaurants-in-charlotte-nc/" data-jpibfi-post-title="7 Best Restaurants in Charlotte, NC [2026 Updated]" data-jpibfi- ></p><p>We have a slideshow of memories in our brain that always appear when we can’t sleep. It’s typically a medley of flashbacks of our most cringe moments over the years, to TikTok songs we’ve heard too many times, and always, without fail, the time we tripped up in our primary school assembly. But sometimes, on a good day, we see images of this Tomahawk steak. To call it impressive would be a huge understatement. It feels more like a love letter to beef.</p><p>Perfectly cooked, with a rich crust and tender center, it’s juicy, it’s bold, and it’s the closest you’ll get to a carnivore’s dream.</p><p><iframe width="100%" height="300" style="border:0;" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed/v1/place?q=place_id:ChIJeeL4ziSgVogR9noAgsMYhUk&amp;zoom=17&amp;key=AIzaSyDhhWij3suiM7Ju7qOcU66HY61rNBu8JRk"></iframe></p><div style="border-bottom: 1px solid #d9d9d9; margin: 16px 0;"></div><h2>Maiz Agua Sal</h2><p>$$ | <a href="tel:(704) 910-6010" rel="nofollow">(704) 910-6010</a> | <a href="http://mastortilleria.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">WEBSITE</a></p><p><img class="aligncenter br-lazy" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0naHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmcnIHZpZXdCb3g9JzAgMCAwIDAnPjwvc3ZnPg==" data-breeze="https://restaurantobserver.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Maiz-Agua-Sal.jpeg"  alt='Maiz Agua Sal' src='https://restaurantobserver.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Maiz-Agua-Sal.jpeg' data-jpibfi-post-excerpt="" data-jpibfi-post-url="https://restaurantobserver.com/restaurants-in-charlotte-nc/" data-jpibfi-post-title="7 Best Restaurants in Charlotte, NC [2026 Updated]" data-jpibfi- ></p><p>The average price for a meal at Maiz Agua Sal is around $18, which feels just right for the kind of vibrant, flavorful experience you’re getting. We know this because it’s physically impossible to take a bite of the trio of salsas without developing an intense curiosity for the source of the bold, smoky flavors you’re consuming. Except this merry expedition down a flavor hole is driven on by an infatuation for a naughty and tender little mouthful of food.</p><p>Highly-addictive yet gloriously simple, Maiz Agua Sal have effectively looked at traditional Mexican ingredients and thought ‘how do we make them socially acceptable to serve in a casual, welcoming dining room’. The answer? Present them with care and confidence. We salute them.</p><p><iframe width="100%" height="300" style="border:0;" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed/v1/place?q=place_id:ChIJkfUpMLuhVogRPskzOsoLR4M&amp;zoom=17&amp;key=AIzaSyDhhWij3suiM7Ju7qOcU66HY61rNBu8JRk"></iframe></p><div style="border-bottom: 1px solid #d9d9d9; margin: 16px 0;"></div><h2>Belfast Mill Irish Pub</h2><p>$ | <a href="tel:(704) 333-7160" rel="nofollow">(704) 333-7160</a> | <a href="http://www.belfastmillclt.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">WEBSITE</a></p><p><img class="aligncenter br-lazy" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0naHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmcnIHZpZXdCb3g9JzAgMCAwIDAnPjwvc3ZnPg==" data-breeze="https://restaurantobserver.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Belfast-Mill-Irish-Pub.jpeg"  alt='Belfast Mill Irish Pub' src='https://restaurantobserver.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Belfast-Mill-Irish-Pub.jpeg' data-jpibfi-post-excerpt="" data-jpibfi-post-url="https://restaurantobserver.com/restaurants-in-charlotte-nc/" data-jpibfi-post-title="7 Best Restaurants in Charlotte, NC [2026 Updated]" data-jpibfi- ></p><p>First thing’s first, the Guinness is cold and smooth. Crisp with a hint of bitterness underneath. But let’s not beat around the bush here. Belfast Mill serves up posh pints. POSH PINTS. Of course, pints should never be made posh. But when it happens, it’s very exciting and, it turns out, also very delicious. Their house ale is a solid, dependable drink, after all.</p><p>Only they come with a side of friendly banter and a welcoming smile from Zach, the staff member who knows your name before you’ve even ordered. Take note, local bars.</p><p><iframe width="100%" height="300" style="border:0;" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed/v1/place?q=place_id:ChIJT6HzRcUfVIgR9TxLTL7c3Sg&amp;zoom=17&amp;key=AIzaSyDhhWij3suiM7Ju7qOcU66HY61rNBu8JRk"></iframe></p><div style="border-bottom: 1px solid #d9d9d9; margin: 16px 0;"></div><h2>The Peace Pipe</h2><p>$$ | <a href="tel:(980) 859-0838" rel="nofollow">(980) 859-0838</a> | <a href="http://www.thepeacepipe.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">WEBSITE</a></p><p><img class="aligncenter br-lazy" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0naHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmcnIHZpZXdCb3g9JzAgMCAwIDAnPjwvc3ZnPg==" data-breeze="https://restaurantobserver.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/The-Peace-Pipe.jpeg"  alt='The Peace Pipe' src='https://restaurantobserver.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/The-Peace-Pipe.jpeg' data-jpibfi-post-excerpt="" data-jpibfi-post-url="https://restaurantobserver.com/restaurants-in-charlotte-nc/" data-jpibfi-post-title="7 Best Restaurants in Charlotte, NC [2026 Updated]" data-jpibfi- ></p><p>You might associate The Peace Pipe with hookah and a laid-back vibe, but it’s also one of the best places in Charlotte to unwind with a drink and some good music. Here they let the atmosphere do all the talking, because when it’s as cozy and chill as this one is, it doesn’t need any other frills. Sipping on a $5 ‘u saw’ while lounging on a plush sofa, you won’t find much else to distract you. The décor is simple but inviting—think soft lighting, wooden accents, and plenty of space to spread out.</p><p>Though the service can be hit or miss, with bartenders sometimes slow to check in and a few rude encounters, the friendly hookah girl and attentive security staff make up for it. On certain nights, half-price hookahs add an extra reason to stay late and enjoy the relaxed, open-air feel.</p><p><iframe width="100%" height="300" style="border:0;" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed/v1/place?q=place_id:ChIJ2T-H4yafVogRCtsr480sC-Q&amp;zoom=17&amp;key=AIzaSyDhhWij3suiM7Ju7qOcU66HY61rNBu8JRk"></iframe></p><div style="border-bottom: 1px solid #d9d9d9; margin: 16px 0;"></div><h2>Shake Shack Blakeney</h2><p>$ | <a href="tel:(980) 221-1821" rel="nofollow">(980) 221-1821</a> | <a href="https://www.shakeshack.com/location/blakeney-nc" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">WEBSITE</a></p><p><img class="aligncenter br-lazy" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0naHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmcnIHZpZXdCb3g9JzAgMCAwIDAnPjwvc3ZnPg==" data-breeze="https://restaurantobserver.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shake-Shack-Blakeney.jpeg"  alt='Shake Shack Blakeney' src='https://restaurantobserver.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shake-Shack-Blakeney.jpeg' data-jpibfi-post-excerpt="" data-jpibfi-post-url="https://restaurantobserver.com/restaurants-in-charlotte-nc/" data-jpibfi-post-title="7 Best Restaurants in Charlotte, NC [2026 Updated]" data-jpibfi- ></p><p>Families seeking a quick yet satisfying meal in Charlotte will find a reliable spot at Shake Shack Blakeney. The menu offers a variety of burgers, fries, and Korean chicken sandwiches, with the Korean BBQ Burger &#038; Fries standing out as a must-try. While the ordering is done via a self-serve kiosk, the staff—led by a friendly server named Daniel—still manages to provide fast and attentive service, often explaining the menu with a smile.</p><p>The atmosphere is casual and welcoming, with outdoor seating that makes it ideal for a relaxed lunch or dinner. A nearby play area adds to its appeal for parents looking for a place where kids can burn off some energy while they eat. It’s not a fine dining experience, but for a quick bite with a side of convenience, it hits all the right notes.</p><p><iframe width="100%" height="300" style="border:0;" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed/v1/place?q=place_id:ChIJEw31lsUpVIgRoCiJdd1vjh8&amp;zoom=17&amp;key=AIzaSyDhhWij3suiM7Ju7qOcU66HY61rNBu8JRk"></iframe></p><div style="border-bottom: 1px solid #d9d9d9; margin: 16px 0;"></div><h2>Bulla Gastrobar</h2><p>$$ | <a href="tel:(704) 837-4422" rel="nofollow">(704) 837-4422</a> | <a href="https://bullagastrobar.com/locations/charlotte/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">WEBSITE</a></p><p><img class="aligncenter br-lazy" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0naHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmcnIHZpZXdCb3g9JzAgMCAwIDAnPjwvc3ZnPg==" data-breeze="https://restaurantobserver.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Bulla-Gastrobar.jpeg"  alt='Bulla Gastrobar' src='https://restaurantobserver.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Bulla-Gastrobar.jpeg' data-jpibfi-post-excerpt="" data-jpibfi-post-url="https://restaurantobserver.com/restaurants-in-charlotte-nc/" data-jpibfi-post-title="7 Best Restaurants in Charlotte, NC [2026 Updated]" data-jpibfi- ></p><p>If you’re looking for a place that feels like it’s been quietly perfecting its craft for years, Bulla Gastrobar is the kind of spot that makes you wonder why you haven’t been here sooner. The honey-glazed burger is a standout, with just the right balance of sweet and savory, and the grilled octopus is tender enough to make even the most skeptical diner pause. The brioche dessert with almond ice cream and honey is a highlight, though some might wish for a little more honey to really bring it home.</p><p>The pan con tomate is another must-try, simple but deeply satisfying. The servers are friendly and attentive, though recent reports of longer wait times and inconsistent service have made their way through the neighborhood. Still, the patio remains a lovely spot to linger over a meal, and the in-house potato chips are crisp and light—perfect for sharing.</p><p>With a menu that leans into both vegetarian and meat lovers, and a vibe that’s both lively and welcoming, Bulla Gastrobar continues to be a go-to for those who value good food and a bit of charm.</p><p><iframe width="100%" height="300" style="border:0;" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed/v1/place?q=place_id:ChIJSfu95KqfVogROiZgXVyrg5A&amp;zoom=17&amp;key=AIzaSyDhhWij3suiM7Ju7qOcU66HY61rNBu8JRk"></iframe></p><div class="crp_related     crp-text-only"><h3>Related Posts:</h3><ul><li><a href="https://restaurantobserver.com/seafood-restaurants-in-charlotte-nc/"     class="crp_link post-1917"><span class="crp_title">12 Best Seafood Restaurants in Charlotte, NC [2026 Updated]</span></a></li><li><a href="https://restaurantobserver.com/italian-restaurants-charlotte-north-carolina/"     class="crp_link post-3890"><span class="crp_title">15 Best Italian Restaurants in Charlotte, NC [2026 Updated]</span></a></li><li><a href="https://restaurantobserver.com/restaurants-charlotte-north-carolina/"     class="crp_link post-2851"><span class="crp_title">12 Best Restaurants in Charlotte, NC</span></a></li></ul><div class="crp_clear"></div></div><div class="swp_social_panel swp_horizontal_panel swp_flat_fresh  swp_default_full_color swp_individual_full_color swp_other_full_color scale-100  scale-" data-min-width="1100" data-float-color="#ffffff" data-float="none" data-float-mobile="none" data-transition="slide" data-post-id="176101" ><div class="nc_tweetContainer swp_share_button swp_twitter" data-network="twitter"><a class="nc_tweet swp_share_link" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" href="https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=7+Best+Restaurants+in+Charlotte%2C+NC+%5B2026+Updated%5D&url=https%3A%2F%2Frestaurantobserver.com%2Frestaurants-in-charlotte-nc%2F" data-link="https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=7+Best+Restaurants+in+Charlotte%2C+NC+%5B2026+Updated%5D&url=https%3A%2F%2Frestaurantobserver.com%2Frestaurants-in-charlotte-nc%2F"><span class="swp_count swp_hide"><span class="iconFiller"><span class="spaceManWilly"><i class="sw swp_twitter_icon"></i><span class="swp_share">Tweet</span></span></span></span></a></div><div class="nc_tweetContainer swp_share_button swp_facebook" data-network="facebook"><a class="nc_tweet swp_share_link" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.facebook.com/share.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Frestaurantobserver.com%2Frestaurants-in-charlotte-nc%2F" data-link="https://www.facebook.com/share.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Frestaurantobserver.com%2Frestaurants-in-charlotte-nc%2F"><span class="